second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"When was Carl Roth born?\", \"slot_hint\": \"birth_date\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 130, \"text\": \"Carl Reinhold Roth Carl Reinhold Roth was a Swedish businessman and ironmaster who lived during the late 17th to mid 18th century.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d00\", \"start\": 131, \"end\": 219, \"text\": \"He is best known as the first ironmaster named Roth at the ironworks in Ludvika, Sweden.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d00\", \"start\": 220, \"end\": 291, \"text\": \"Reinhold was in his time one of Stockholm's more prominent businessmen.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d00\", \"start\": 292, \"end\": 510, \"text\": \"He also owned Sunnansjö ironworks and estate, and Skogsegen (Judge Hörneåfor’s ironworks in Västerbotten), devoted himself to the nascent sawmill industry, and was ship-owner of the Augusta (named for his second wife).\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d00\", \"start\": 511, \"end\": 563, \"text\": \"Reinhold was born November 18, 1797 in Lower Fösked.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d00\", \"start\": 564, \"end\": 619, \"text\": \"His career began in Stockholm, where he was employed by\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 111, \"text\": \"Carl Reinhold Roth was a Swedish businessman and ironmaster who lived during the late 17th to mid 18th century.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d01\", \"start\": 112, \"end\": 200, \"text\": \"He is best known as the first ironmaster named Roth at the ironworks in Ludvika, Sweden.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d01\", \"start\": 201, \"end\": 272, \"text\": \"Reinhold was in his time one of Stockholm's more prominent businessmen.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d01\", \"start\": 273, \"end\": 491, \"text\": \"He also owned Sunnansjö ironworks and estate, and Skogsegen (Judge Hörneåfor’s ironworks in Västerbotten), devoted himself to the nascent sawmill industry, and was ship-owner of the Augusta (named for his second wife).\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d01\", \"start\": 492, \"end\": 542, \"text\": \"Reinhold was born January 1, 1800 in Lower Fösked.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d01\", \"start\": 543, \"end\": 598, \"text\": \"His career began in Stockholm, where he was employed by\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 97, \"text\": \"Carl Roth II Carl Roth II was a Swedish ironmaster who lived between the 17th and 18th centuries.\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d02\", \"start\": 98, \"end\": 234, \"text\": \"He is best known for owning two ironworks in Karlstad Municipality, Värmland County, Sweden: Duvnäs (Duvenäs), and Nedre Fösked (Föske).\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d02\", \"start\": 235, \"end\": 283, \"text\": \"Carl was born on October 12, 1753, in Stockholm.\"}, \"D3S4\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d02\", \"start\": 284, \"end\": 379, \"text\": \"On June 26, 1764, at the age of 10, he enrolled at Uppsala University under Stockholm's Nation.\"}, \"D3S5\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d02\", \"start\": 380, \"end\": 533, \"text\": \"After graduating in 1771, he moved with his parents to their estate at Duvnäs where he focused primarily on agriculture and working at the family's mill.\"}, \"D3S6\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d02\", \"start\": 534, \"end\": 586, \"text\": \"Carl was said to have a Godly and humble disposition\"}, \"D4S1\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d03\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 121, \"text\": \"Carl Roth (basketball) Carl William Roth (September 15, 1909 – May 28, 1966) was an American basketball player and coach.\"}, \"D4S2\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d03\", \"start\": 122, \"end\": 267, \"text\": \"A native of Sheboygan, Wisconsin, Roth attended the University of Wisconsin–Madison and played for their men's basketball team from 1929 to 1932.\"}, \"D4S3\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d03\", \"start\": 268, \"end\": 366, \"text\": \"Six years later he played in 14 total games for the Sheboygan Red Skins during the 1938–39 season.\"}, \"D4S4\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d03\", \"start\": 367, \"end\": 465, \"text\": \"The Red Skins were a professional franchise that competed in the National Basketball League (NBL).\"}, \"D4S5\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d03\", \"start\": 466, \"end\": 571, \"text\": \"Roth stayed with the team as both its legal counsel and in other capacities after his one season playing.\"}, \"D4S6\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d03\", \"start\": 572, \"end\": 598, \"text\": \"He took over as head coach\"}, \"D5S1\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d04\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 624, \"text\": \"Charles II | Biography , Accomplishments , & Facts | Britannica Search Britannica Click here to search Search Britannica Click here to search SUBSCRIBE Login SUBSCRIBE Home History & Society Science & Tech Biographies Animals & Nature Geography & Travel Arts & Culture ProCon Money Games & Quizzes Videos On This Day One Good Fact Dictionary New Articles History & Society Lifestyles & Social Issues Philosophy & Religion Politics , Law & Government World History Science & Tech Health & Medicine Science Technology Biographies Browse Biographies Animals & Nature Birds , Reptiles & Other Vertebrates Bugs , Mollusks & Other\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Carl Reinhold Roth\", \"scope\": \"Birth date\", \"claim\": \"Reinhold was born November 18, 1797 in Lower Fösked.\", \"answer\": \"November 18, 1797\", \"quote\": \"Reinhold was born November 18, 1797 in Lower Fösked.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"Carl Reinhold Roth\", \"scope\": \"Birth date\", \"claim\": \"Reinhold was born January 1, 1800 in Lower Fösked.\", \"answer\": \"January 1, 1800\", \"quote\": \"Reinhold was born January 1, 1800 in Lower Fösked.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d02\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d02:c0\", \"entity\": \"Carl Roth\", \"scope\": \"Birth date\", \"claim\": \"Carl was born on October 12, 1753, in Stockholm.\", \"answer\": \"October 12, 1753\", \"quote\": \"Carl was born on October 12, 1753, in Stockholm.\", \"original_document_number\": 3}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d03\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0442-9468acb685ff:d03:c0\", \"entity\": \"Carl Roth\", \"scope\": \"birth date\", \"claim\": \"Carl William Roth was born on September 15, 1909.\", \"answer\": \"September 15, 1909\", \"quote\": \"Carl Roth (basketball) Carl William Roth (September 15, 1909 – May 28, 1966) was an American basketball pl